# Senior Engineering SOLID Rule

Training SoT (chi tiết): `_vibe-team-os/25-SOLID-AND-CODING-CONVENTION.md`  
Dev lanes FE/BE/Mobile: `_vibe-team-os/26-DEV-LANES-WEB-MOBILE-BE.md`  
Project read map: `docs/program/SUBAGENT_READ_MAP.md` · `AGENTS.md`

Apply this rule to all implementation and refactoring work.

## SOLID baseline
- **S (Single Responsibility):** each module/class/function has one clear reason to change.
- **O (Open/Closed):** extend behavior via composition/abstraction, avoid risky edits to stable cores.
- **L (Liskov Substitution):** subtype behavior must remain contract-compatible.
- **I (Interface Segregation):** prefer small focused interfaces over large generic contracts.
- **D (Dependency Inversion):** depend on abstractions at boundaries, not concrete infrastructure details.

## Senior code quality checks
- Keep domain logic separated from transport/framework concerns.
- Prefer explicit contracts and deterministic error semantics.
- Design for testability: seams, mocks/stubs, and observable outcomes.
- Minimize coupling and hidden global state.
- Document non-obvious trade-offs in decision records.

## Anti-patterns (reject)
- God objects/modules with mixed responsibilities.
- Business logic buried in controllers/views.
- Tight coupling to external SDKs across core domain.
- Large functions with implicit side effects and no tests.
- FE joining multiple API entities into a domain aggregate, payroll/insurance formulas on FE, or FE-built nested write DTOs (see OS `25` §3.1 · `26` §7 · SoT `28-FE-BE-SEPARATION-DISPLAY-READY.md`).
- Missing `solid_convention_ack` FE–BE boundary / display-ready fields on list-mutate waves.

## Acceptance
- No major change marked DONE without SOLID-oriented review notes.
- Refactors must reduce complexity or improve reliability measurably.
